Source: dragomand
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Blagovest Petrov <blagovest@petrovs.info>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13),
 cargo,
 rustc (>= 1.85),
 cmake (>= 3.25),
 ninja-build,
 g++,
 pkgconf,
 libpcre2-dev,
 libblas-dev,
 liblapack-dev,
 dbus-daemon
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Homepage: https://dragomand.l10n-bg.dev
Vcs-Browser: https://github.com/VuteTech/dragomand
Vcs-Git: https://github.com/VuteTech/dragomand.git
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: dragomand
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends},
 default-dbus-session-bus | dbus-session-bus
Recommends: libopenblas0
Suggests: wl-clipboard | xclip, libnotify-bin
Description: offline machine translation daemon for the desktop
 Dragomand is a per-user daemon that gives desktop applications fully
 offline machine translation over D-Bus. It runs Mozilla's
 Bergamot/Marian translation models (the ones behind Firefox
 Translations) locally, downloads and verifies models on demand, keeps
 recently used pairs warm within a memory budget, and exits when idle.
 .
 The package ships the D-Bus activated daemon, the dragomanctl command
 line client, and the KRunner and GNOME Shell search services.
